    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="0724" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.62114A/4–1845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-18T20:00:00+03:00">April 18, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 18—1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1244. We have received no reply to the Ambassador’s letter to Molotov dated April
                    15, which was sent in compliance with Department’s 864 April 14, noon.<anchor
                        n="10" xml:id="d504-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Under the circumstances I am informing Foreign Office that we are proceeding with
                    the acceptance of the German proposal insofar as it relates to American
                    prisoners of war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennan</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d504-f1" n="10" xml:id="d504-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 864 not printed, but see telegram 1486, April 14, to Paris, <ref
                        target="#pg712">p. 712</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
